window.docContents[9].resolve({"/Verification/Mind-the-Fibration-Gap/#engineering-rule":{"contents":"When engineering a headline theorem intended for dependency-analysis\nconsumption:\n\n1. Expose the fibration in the type.  Name the pipeline functions\nexplicitly in the statement; avoid Prop-wrappers that hide them.2. Cite lemmas about callees.  Every project lemma used in the\nproof should itself be about a function that is a strict callee\nof the function the root theorem is about.3. Prefer a step-wise proof over a tactic blob.  Each\nhave ⟨…⟩ := lemma … contributes one functorial step;\neach uncited unfold/split/grind discards one.\n\n","context":"L4YAML: A Verified YAML 1.2.2 Parser in Lean 4\u0009Verification\u0009Mind the Fibration Gap","header":"3.5.4. The Engineering Rule","id":"/Verification/Mind-the-Fibration-Gap/#engineering-rule"}});